W AX3051 1463-callback-restrictions.ax:5:6-11 restriction-unverifiable "`apply` claims `restrict(no-io)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body CALLS its own parameter `f`, so what it performs is decided by the argument each caller passes - the effect row is complete about this body and says nothing about that call" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast`, `no-wrap` and `no-trap` are checked regardless, because all three are lexical and need no call resolved"
E AX3049 1463-callback-restrictions.ax:32:8-14 restriction-violated "this callback may perform IO; apply requires no-io" ?"pass a callback that keeps the restriction"
